  "id": "1434fd45-ba5c-4d5f-877c-5ffced5b369b",
  "title": "RBI and Fed Amid Inflation and Rate Hikes",
  "summary": "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) reiterated its support for the Indian rupee amid rising oil prices, while the Federal Reserve (Fed) raised concerns about inflation and potential rate hikes. The Indian inflation rate rose, and the US Federal Reserve faced mixed signals regarding rate adjustments.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "RBI Governor Sanjay Malhotra preferred to wait for greater certainty on the inflation trajectory as he and other MPC members voted to maintain the existing interest rate earlier this month.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "India's retail inflation rose to 4.45% in July, driven by higher food prices, while economists expect no immediate rate hike despite rising upside risks.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The US Federal Reserve faced mixed signals from recent July payrolls and job data, with weak figures providing some cover for its rate adjustments, while a disappointing job report left investors uncertain.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
